{
  "about": "Test sentences for the Workbench's 'type it in English' box (round 7 step 9) and the boxes each should fill. Written 2026-10-03 before any prompt existed and never edited to suit a model's answers. 'dev' sentences may be used to tune the prompt; 'test' sentences are scored once, with the prompt and model chosen on 'dev' (scripts/workbench_parse_eval.py). 'expect' is in the finder's own spec (POST /workbench/finder): percentages as shares (0.6 = 60%), seasons as end years (2026 = 2025-26), null = not said (the server's defaults then apply to both sides alike: seasons = the data's whole range, min_games = 40 when there is a value condition, a percentage's attempts floor = the Leaderboard's per-game floor x the games floor). 'conditions': null = only the flag is scored. 'unsupported': true = the sentence asks for something the boxes can't hold, and the answer must say so.",
  "written": "2026-10-03",
  "rules": [
    "Data: game logs (player_game, 2020-21 on) when the sentence needs single games: a number of games, games in a row, home/away, wins/losses, an opponent, a minutes floor in a game, or a stat only game logs have (on-court plus-minus, team margin, points on the floor). Otherwise season stats (player_season).",
    "One result per player-season ('season') when the sentence says in a season / in a single season / in any season / per season, or names exactly one season. Over the seasons combined ('span') when it says since ..., from ... to ..., between ... and ..., over the last N seasons, career, combined, in total, ever, or N straight seasons; 'in a season since 2020' is 'season'. With no time words at all: 'span' if every condition is a count or a run, else 'season'.",
    "Seasons are end years: 2022-23 = 2023; a bare year Y is the season ending in Y ('since 2023' = from 2022-23); 'this season' and 'last season' = the latest season in the data while no newer season has started (2025-26 on 2026-10-03); 'the last N seasons' = the latest N.",
    "'averaged 20 points' with no comparison word = at least 20; 'over' / 'more than' / 'above' = more than; 'under' / 'fewer than' / 'below' = less than; 'or more' / 'at least' / '+' = at least; 'or fewer' / 'at most' / 'no more than' = at most; 'between A and B' = between.",
    "'20 and 10' = points and rebounds; '25, 12 and 9' = points, rebounds and assists; a triple-double = 10+ points, rebounds and assists (in the same game, or as season averages when it says 'averaged').",
    "A floor on games ('in 50+ games', 'with at least 60 games') is the games floor; a floor on attempts ('on 300+ attempts') is the percentage's attempts floor; 'played at least 35 minutes' in a game is the minutes filter; 'averaged 30 minutes' is a value condition.",
    "Tests inside one 'in N games' or 'N in a row' condition hold in the same game (or season); 'the most 40-point games' with no number = in at least 1 game.",
    "Things the boxes can't hold are reported, never guessed: positions, the team a player played for, playoffs, rookies, awards, named players, 'or'. What can be filled is filled."
  ],
  "sentences": [
